---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Jake Reddy"
  description="Full-Stack Software Engineer. Language-agnostic, fundamentals-driven engineering."
>
  <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 py-10 md:px-8 md:py-16 lg:px-12 lg:py-20">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold mb-10 md:text-5xl">About</h1>

    <!-- Section 1: Background -->
    <section class="mb-10 md:mb-14">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Background</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-base text-[#595959] dark:text-[#A3A3A3] leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I am a Full-Stack Software Engineer with experience spanning distributed systems, API
        backends, and frontend web applications. I work across the entire software lifecycle — from
        designing database schemas and system architecture to shipping responsive user interfaces. I
        thrive in environments with clear ownership and non-negotiable quality standards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Philosophy -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#E5E5E5] dark:border-[#333333] pt-8 mb-10 md:mb-14">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-base text-[#595959] dark:text-[#A3A3A3] leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        To me, programming languages and frameworks are tools — specific syntax is secondary to
        underlying computer science fundamentals, system design, and problem-solving. Software
        should be as simple as the problem allows and no simpler. I value legibility, reliable
        engineering, and building maintainable systems that outlast framework trends.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Nordic Life -->
    <section class="border-t border-[#E5E5E5] pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Nordic Life</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-base text-[#595959] leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I am based in Oslo, Norway, and have lived in the Nordic countries for the past four years.
        The directness, the long winters that demand indoor focus, and the cultural respect for
        craftsmanship all align with how I prefer to work. I am available across European time zones
        and collaborate regularly with distributed teams in the UK, Germany, and Sweden.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
